    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n66388" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέση</span></b>  (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χορδή</span>), ἡ, the <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>mese</i>, i. e. the top note of the lower
			tetrachord in the octave, originally the <i>middle string</i> of
			the seven-stringed (or of an earlier three-stringed) lyre, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				443d
			</span></i> (cf. Sch.), <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Metaph.</u>
				1018b29
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Pr.</u>
				919b20
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Euc.
				<u>Sect.Can.</u>
				10
			</span></i>; variously defined, <i><span class="en">
				Ptol.
				<u>Harm.</u>
				2.5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Cleonid.
				<u>Harm.</u>
				11
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Bacch.
				<u>Harm.</u>
				65
			</span></i>:—
				Dor.
			
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέσσα</span></b> 
			<i><span class="en">
				Philol.
				6
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> Geom.,
				<i>mean proportional</i>, 
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέσος</span>
			 III. <i><span class="en">
				5
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> in
			punctuation (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στιγμή</span>), dot
			placed midway between top and bottom of line, functioning as a
				<i>comma</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Satyr.
				6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.T.
				630.6
			</span></i>, Sch.D.T.<i><span class="en">
				p.177
			</span></i> H.</div>
